rent (verification) oversight (audit) by a global community, empower individuals by giving them choice and visibility into how AI systems function, rather than relying on an opaque, centralized authority. This approach truly protects autonomy (individual/data) by empowering users, rather than by stifling the very technology that can liberate humanity.\n\nThe real threat to human liberation is not data aggregation, but the centralized control over powerful AI, whether by governments or corporations. As machine vision technology is currently used for surveillance that is biased against minorities, the solution is not to hobble the technology, but to democratize its development and deployment. \"Marc Andreessen Manifesto Says AI Regulation â€œIs a Form of Murderâ€ \" clearly articulates that the moral cost of inaction—of delaying life-saving AI—is immense. We must accelerate capability development via decentralized accountability, fostering a competitive environment where open-source proliferation drives both innovation and safety, rather than allowing a fear of the unknown to condemn humanity to preventable suffering and scarcity. We need to unleash AI to solve humanity's grand challenges now, not slow it down with bureaucratic friction that will inevitably fail.",
